From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:05:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: A maximized window whose screen went away is
 arranged anew

When a screen goes away, e.g. the virtual one when the VNC desktop ends,
its windows were only moved to the remaining screen. A maximized window
kept the size it had there. The next commit with that size, an app that
plays music commits all the time, then took it for the client's answer:
scale-to-fit divided the phone's usable area by the desktop's window
size, the scale ended at its floor of 0.5, and that scale confirmed
itself from then on. The app stayed in its desktop layout at half size.

A maximized window is now arranged on the remaining screen, which starts
its scale over from the client's minimum size. Any other window moves to
that screen like one moved there by hand: on the phone it is maximized.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/desktop.c | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/desktop.c b/src/desktop.c
index 5596056e..99199b9c 100644
--- a/src/desktop.c
+++ b/src/desktop.c
@@ -419,8 +419,7 @@ phoc_desktop_view_check_visibility (PhocDesktop *self, PhocView *view)
 
 
 struct move_to_layout_space_data {
-  double center_x;
-  double center_y;
+  PhocOutput *output;
 };
 
 
@@ -436,7 +435,15 @@ move_to_layout_space_iter (PhocDesktop *self, PhocView *view, gpointer user_data
 
   /* Its screen went away (e.g. the virtual one when VNC ends): keep its geometry there */
   phoc_view_remember_geometry (view);
-  phoc_view_move (view, data->center_x - box.width / 2, data->center_y - box.height / 2);
+
+  /* A maximized view only moved would keep the size it had there. Its next commit would then
+   * judge that size against the new screen and scale the view down for good, see
+   * view_reset_scale(). Arranged anew it gets the size and scale of the new screen. */
+  if (phoc_view_is_maximized (view))
+    phoc_view_arrange (view, data->output, TRUE);
+  else
+    phoc_view_move_to_output (view, data->output);
+
   return TRUE;
 }
 
@@ -446,8 +453,6 @@ handle_layout_change (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
 {
   PhocDesktop *self;
   struct wlr_output *center_output;
-  struct wlr_box center_output_box;
-  double center_x, center_y;
   PhocOutput *output;
 
   self = wl_container_of (listener, self, layout_change);
@@ -455,16 +460,11 @@ handle_layout_change (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
   if (center_output == NULL)
     return;
 
-  wlr_output_layout_get_box (self->layout, center_output, &center_output_box);
-  center_x = center_output_box.x + center_output_box.width / 2;
-  center_y = center_output_box.y + center_output_box.height / 2;
-
   /* Make sure all views are on an existing output */
   phoc_desktop_for_each_view (self,
                               move_to_layout_space_iter,
                                (gpointer)&(struct move_to_layout_space_data) {
-                                 .center_x = center_x,
-                                 .center_y = center_y,
+                                 .output = PHOC_OUTPUT (center_output->data),
                                });
 
   /* Damage all outputs since the move above damaged old layout space */
